# Best coding practices (admin-dashboard)

- Write clear, maintainable, testable code in small, focused units.
- Prefer readability over clever shortcuts; match existing file style and naming.
- Keep components and functions single-purpose; extract shared helpers when duplication appears.
- Handle errors explicitly; use user-safe messages and fallbacks for API failures.
- Keep side effects predictable (effects with correct dependencies, no stale closures in auth flows).
- Remove dead code and unused imports.
- Add brief comments only when business or RBAC logic is non-obvious.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested feature; avoid unrelated refactors.

## Project conventions

- Reuse shared UI from `@/components/common`, `@/components/branding`, and `@/components/data`.
- Use MUI `sx` and theme palette tokens; avoid scattered raw hex except in `src/theme/`.
- Call the backend through `@/api/apiClient` and named endpoints in `@/api/apiEndpoints.js` (not raw `fetch` in screens).
